This text-xs/amber-600 pairing is unchanged code (same Tailwind classes
existed in the old, dead outer copy) — but S4 is precisely what makes this
element render for a real user for the first time. A contrast failure in
dead code is moot; the same failure in now-live code is a point 7 violation
this task is responsible for surfacing, whether or not S4 introduced the
class names.

